-- title:
--   Index of Γ∩ s⁻¹Γ s in Γ equals the Hecke arrow degree
-- statement:
--   Let $a_1,b_1$ be rational numbers and $N,q,q'$ natural numbers with $N$ non-zero and squarefree, $q$ and $q'$ prime, $q'\neq q$, $q,q'\geq 5$ and $q\nmid N$, $q'\nmid N$. Assume $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and that for a maximal ideal $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra precisely when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1$ be a maximal $\mathbb Z$-order (an order, in the sense of a finitely generated $\mathbb Z$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication and spanning the algebra over $\mathbb Q$, maximal among the orders containing it) and let $R_1\leq\Lambda_1$ be an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. an intersection $\Lambda'\cap\Lambda''$ of two maximal orders with additive relative index $N$ in $\Lambda'$. Let $n_1$ be a unit of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ lying in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $q$: $n_1$ and $q\,n_1^{-1}$ lie in the finite adelic box of $R_1$, while $n_1^{-1}$ and $q^{-1}n_1$ do not; assume the meet order $R_1\cap\mathrm{conj}_{n_1}(R_1)$ is an Eichler order of level $Nq$. Let $v_2$ be a maximal ideal containing $q$, let $\ell$ be a prime different from $q$ and $q'$, and let $s$ be a global unit and $sf$ an adelic unit such that the component of $sf$ at every $u$ with $q\notin u$ is $s\otimes 1$, its component at every $u$ with $q\in u$ is $1$, the element $\ell\cdot sf^{-1}$ (with $\ell$ embedded diagonally through the centre) lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` if $\ell\mid N$ — that is, in the prime Hecke set at $\ell$ of the meet order, with the further requirements that conjugation by it moves the meet order and that the meet order is not contained in the conjugate of $\Lambda_1$ — and in the prime Hecke set of the meet order at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s)=\ell$. Let $\Gamma$ be the subgroup consisting of those units $x$ whose image in $(\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w)^\times$ lies in the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$ for every maximal ideal $w\neq v_2$, and for which $v_q(\mathrm{nrd}(x))$ is even. Then the index of $\Gamma\cap s^{-1}\Gamma s$ in $\Gamma$ equals $\ell$ if $\ell\mid N$ and $\ell+1$ otherwise; this is the value of `HeckeTower.arrowDegree N (ℓ,1)`, which depends only on $\ell$ and $N$ and not on the `Fin 2` tag.
--
--   Classically this is the degree of one of the two degeneracy maps attached to the Hecke correspondence at $\ell$ on a Shimura curve of level $N$ coming from a definite quaternion algebra, expressed as an index of arithmetic groups in the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset-graph model. It supports the companion statement for the tag-$0$ conjugation and the construction of the quotient presentation of the class set together with the realisation statements for the Hecke tower.
